    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked for membership level 4 to require tenure of more than 365 days, while a brand-new owner (zero tenure) stays capped at level 3.\n\nThe only place `membershipLevel` is derived is `MembershipLevels.forOwner`, wired into `OwnerMapper` via a MapStruct expression. Previously it computed level from email (+1) and `namesakeCount == 0` (+1) and hard-capped at 3 \u2014 so level 4 was documented as \"reserved for tenure\" but unreachable.\n\nChange made in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/MembershipLevels.java`:\n- The create-time factors (email, namesake) still cap at 3.\n- Added a tenure factor: `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365` bumps the level to 4.\n- A null `registrationDate` (and thus a newly created owner registered today = 0 days tenure) yields 0 tenure, so it never reaches level 4.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` \u2014 a new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` 0, in a 3-member household \u2014 correctly returns level 3, and the whole suite passes.",
